n landing on d2, f6). Aim at their pawn.","tips":["Aim for a steady edge by move 11: 59% of games get there, and 40% reach +6 by move 21.","Watch your knight: it is behind 24% of your lost leads, 1.3\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the queen's knight (59%), landing on d2, f6, f3.","Aim at their pawn: it is behind 24% of their lost leads, most often the b-pawn (30%). The reply wins it outright 16% of the time. Take it with a pawn.","Material changes hands for you on e6 and f6: build pressure there.","They win material on f3 and e3: keep those squares defended.","Look for the trapped piece: it appears 2.5\u00d7 as often as usual in this opening."],"similar":[],"family":"French Defense"}